.TH VLHE.CONF 5 "2026-10-05" "VLHE 1.1.0" "VLHE Manual"
.SH NAME
vlhe.conf \- VLHE settings: the machine's, each user's, and the drive state
.SH DESCRIPTION
VLHE keeps its settings in plain text files of sections and keys:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Sound Settings]
Limiter = 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
A line beginning with
.B ;
or
.B #
is a comment, and blank lines are ignored. Section and key names are
matched without regard to case. Spaces around the
.B =
and at the ends of a value are removed. A key that is absent takes
its default, so a file left exactly as generated behaves as the
software does with no file at all.
.PP
The control centre and
.BR setup-vlhe (8)
write these files. The control centre replaces a file wholesale, with
a comment above every key, so a comment added by hand does not
survive; values edited by hand are kept.
.B setup-vlhe
changes only the keys it offers and leaves the rest of the file,
comments included, as it was. Both keep the previous version as
.IR name .old .
.PP
In the control centre, OK and Apply change the settings in memory
only. They reach these files when File > Save Configuration is used.
.SH THE FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vlhe.conf
The machine's settings: the sections
.BR "[Sound Settings]" ,
.BR "[Midi Settings]" ,
.BR "[CD Settings]" ,
.BR [Tracing] ,
.BR [Boot] ,
.B [Load]
and
.BR [Paths] .
Read at boot and by every load. Writing it needs root.
.TP
.I ~/.vlhe/vlhe.conf
Each user's own settings:
.BR [Interface] ,
.BR "[Render Settings]" ,
.BR "[CDG Viewer]" ,
.BR [Fonts] ,
and the SoundFonts in
.BR "[Midi Settings]" .
Needs no root and affects nobody else.
.TP
.I ~/.vlhe/vlhe-draft.conf
The draft. When a user who cannot write
.I /etc/vlhe.conf
saves, the machine settings go here instead, beside the user's own
file. That user's control centre reads the draft back at its next
start, if it is newer than the system file. Root brings a draft into
the machine's settings with File > Load Configuration, which shows
every change before taking it. File > Save Draft... writes a copy
anywhere, for anyone.
.TP
.I /etc/vlhe/defaults.conf
The settings
.B setup-vlhe
first saved, written once and never changed. Used when
.I /etc/vlhe.conf
is missing, and as the defaults File > Reset Settings goes back to.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vlhe/state/drives
The drive state. See DRIVE STATE below.
.PP
A portable VLHE - built with
.B make portable
(its folder carries a file named
.I PORTABLE
as a label) - keeps its machine settings in that folder's
.IR vlhe.conf ,
each user's in the folder's
.IR vlhe-user- name .conf ,
and its drive state in the folder's
.IR drives .
If the folder cannot be written, a user's settings go to
.I ~/.vlhe/vlhe.conf
instead, and failing that to
.IR /tmp/vlhe- uid /vlhe-user.conf ,
which does not survive a reboot; the control centre says which.
.SH [Sound Settings]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
The mixer, vsound, and its pump,
.BR vsoundd (8).
.TP
.BR LoadAtBoot " (default 1)"
Load the mixer at boot, and at
.BR "vlhe apply" .
Without it nothing else here works.
.TP
.BR Include " (default: as LoadAtBoot)"
Whether the control centre's Load button brings up the mixer - its
Include in load box on the Status page. It does not affect what
boots.
.TP
.BR Channels " (4, not a setting)"
Mixing channels for ordinary programs; a fifth is added for the
synth. Written commented out, because the number is fixed when the
module is built and nothing reads this key.
.TP
.BR MidiChannel " (default 1)"
Reserve a channel for the MIDI synth, so it never competes with
programs for the four. 0 or 1.
.TP
.BR Limiter " (default 1)"
What happens when programs together are louder than the card can
play. 0: off - the sum is clipped. 1: attack and release - the whole
mix is turned down for a loud peak and comes back within a fraction
of a second. 2: soft knee - only the loud samples are bent towards
full scale. Quiet sound passes untouched in every mode.
.TP
.BR Attenuation " (default 100)"
A fixed level for the whole mix, in per cent, applied before the
limiter. 100 is unchanged; 71 is about \-3 dB, 50 about \-6 dB. For a
machine where several loud programs often play at once.
.TP
.BR MixRate " (default 0)"
The rate everything is mixed at, in Hz, passed to
.BR vsoundd (8)
as
.BR \-S .
0 asks the card, which is right almost always; a value outside 8000
to 48000 is treated as 0. Set it only where the card's own answer
cannot be trusted - Corel's packaged emu10k1 driver echoes back any
rate it is asked for, and 48000 is right for that chip. The card
still wins: a rate it cannot do is clamped by its driver, and
.B vsoundd
says so. Takes effect at the next load.
.TP
.BR CardDevice " (default empty)"
The sound card to hear the mix through. Empty means detect, which is
right on a machine with one card. The control centre calls it Play
through. The card is not moved or reloaded.
.TP
.BR ProgramsUse " (default /dev/dsp)"
The device your programs open. While VLHE is loaded it is pointed at
vsound, so anything opening it is mixed rather than taking the card
for itself, and it is put back as it was when VLHE unloads. Change it
only if your programs open another device, such as
.IR /dev/dsp2 .
May be the same device as CardDevice.
.TP
.BR ReleaseOnIdle " (default 0)"
Release the card when the last program stops, so the card's driver
runs its own teardown. Needed for the ESS Solo-1; try it if you hear
a tone when nothing is playing.
.TP
.BR SaveMixerLevels " (default 0)"
Save every sound card's mixer levels when VLHE unloads, and at
shutdown, and put them back when it loads, and at boot. They are kept
in
.IR /var/lib/vlhe/mixers .
.TP
.BR SaveProgramLevels " (default 0)"
Keep each program's level and mute across a reload and a reboot,
in
.IR /var/lib/vlhe/volumes .
Without it a level is still remembered by program name for as long
as vsound stays loaded.
.TP
.BR CardModule " (default empty)"
Read and written by the control centre, but has no effect in this
version.
.SH [Midi Settings]
The synth,
.BR vmidid (8),
and its module. All in
.I /etc/vlhe.conf
except
.B Font0
and
.BR Font1 ,
which are in the user's file.
.TP
.BR LoadAtBoot " (default 1)"
Start the synth at boot, and at
.BR "vlhe apply" .
.TP
.BR Include " (default: as LoadAtBoot)"
Whether the control centre's Load button brings up the synth.
.TP
.BR Font0 ", " Font1 " (default empty)"
In the user's file. The SoundFont the synth plays, as a full path:
.B Font0
is the General MIDI font, in bank 0;
.B Font1
an optional song font, in bank 1. The synth will not start without a
General MIDI font. Set on the Midi Settings page. A user who has set
none gets the machine's,
.B DefaultFont0
and
.BR DefaultFont1 .
.TP
.BR DefaultFont0 ", " DefaultFont1 " (default empty)"
The machine's SoundFonts, in
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf :
what the synth plays at boot, and for a user with no
.B Font0
of their own.
.B DefaultFont0
is the General MIDI font, bank 0;
.B DefaultFont1
an optional bank 1 font. When root chooses fonts on the Midi Settings
page they are written here as well, so root's choice is the machine's.
Without
.B DefaultFont0
the synth cannot start at boot.
.TP
.BR Voices " (default 64)"
The most voices sounding at once, 1 to 512. The synth steals the
quietest when it runs out.
.TP
.BR AutoVoices " (default 1)"
Lower the voice limit by itself while the machine cannot keep up,
and raise it again when it can; never above Voices.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceDrain " (default 50)"
Start reducing while the synth's output buffer averages below this
per cent and is not rising. 5 to 95.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceEmergency " (default 10)"
Below this per cent, end every fading note at once and lower the
limit to what is left. 0 to 90.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceHealthy " (default 75)"
At or above this per cent, and not falling, the full limit comes
back. 10 to 100.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceSettle " (default 100)"
Milliseconds after acting before acting again. 20 to 5000.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceFloor " (default 8)"
Never fewer voices than this. 1 to 64.
.TP
.BR AutoVoiceTails " (default 1)"
1: end notes that are already fading - quietest first, never drums -
before lowering the limit. 0: only lower the limit. Notes still held
are never cut.
.IP
The six AutoVoice settings must keep Emergency less than Drain less
than Healthy, or the whole set is refused and the defaults used. The
Status page's Apply settings gives them to a running synth without a
restart.
.TP
.BR Gain " (default 500)"
The master gain in thousandths: 1000 is unity, 2000 the most.
.TP
.BR Reverb " (default 1)"
The reverb: 1 on, 0 off. It is nearly all of the effects' processor
time, so 0 is the first thing to try on a slow machine.
.TP
.BR Chorus " (default 1)"
The chorus: 1 on, 0 off. Cheap; it can stay on with the reverb off.
Its own setting since 2026-10-05 (it used to follow Reverb).
.TP
.BR Law " (default 0)"
The volume curve: 0 the SoundFont standard, 1 the gentler curve the
OPL3 and original AWE32 drivers used, often better for DOS-era games.
.TP
.BR Filter " (default 0)"
The velocity filter: 0 AWE32, 1 SoundFont 2.01, 2 SoundFont 2.04,
3 none.
.TP
.BR ModEnv " (default 1)"
The modulation envelope: 1 fast, which skips an envelope that modulates
nothing and catches it up exactly when it starts to - less work on a
slow machine; 0 reference, every voice to the SoundFont specification.
Identical on everything tested.
.TP
.BR Rate " (default 44100)"
The synth's sample rate. The control centre offers 44100, 32000,
22050 and 11025. The most effective setting on a slow machine: halving the rate
doubles the time the synth has for each block. Try it before turning
the effects off.
.TP
.BR ChannelRelease " (default 3000)"
Milliseconds of silence - no note sounding and the effects faded -
before the synth lets its sound channel go, so the card can be
released between songs. 0 holds the channel while the synth runs.
.TP
.BR Minor " (default 11)"
The device minor number of
.IR /dev/vmidi .
The control centre offers 7, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14, the numbers no
sound driver on Corel Linux 1.2 uses. Takes effect when vmidi is next
loaded.
.SH [CD Settings]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
The virtual drives, vdisc, and
.BR vdiscd (8).
.TP
.BR LoadAtBoot " (default 1)"
Start the disc daemon at boot, and at
.BR "vlhe apply" .
.TP
.BR Include " (default: as LoadAtBoot)"
Whether the control centre's Load button brings up the drives.
.TP
.BR Drives " (default 1)"
How many virtual drives to create, 1 to 8:
.I /dev/vdisc0
upwards. Takes effect when vdisc is next loaded.
.TP
.BR DrivesAutoLoad " (default 1)"
When the disc daemon starts, put back the image in each drive marked
Load at startup on the CD Settings page. 0: every drive starts empty.
.TP
.BR Major " (default 63)"
The drives' block major number. 60 to 63 are the kernel's range for
devices with no official number. The control centre also offers the
numbers of some period CD-ROM drivers, under Impersonate a period
CD-ROM drive, because cdparanoia recognises drives by them; those
numbers belong to real drivers, and claiming one can stop that
hardware working.
.TP
.BR Packet " (default 1)"
Answer MMC packet commands: needed to rip audio with cdparanoia or
cdda2wav, and to play Video CDs.
.TP
.BR LinkCdrom " (default 0)"
Point
.I /dev/cdrom
at a virtual drive while VLHE is loaded, so CD players and rippers
find it. What it pointed at before is saved and put back at unload.
Which drive it reaches is chosen on the CD Settings page and kept in
the drive state.
.SH [Tracing]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
For a bug report; leave off for normal use.
.TP
.BR Enabled " (default 0)"
1: the next load traces events - opens, closes, settings, refusals.
2: everything, including every CD read and every MIDI byte, which is
very large. The trace goes into each module's own buffer, read through
.IR /proc/vsound-trace ", " /proc/vmidi-trace " and " /proc/vdisc-trace
(or all three in time order with
.BR "vlhe trace" ),
never to the system log. Turn it off again afterwards.
.TP
.BR Capture " (default 0)"
With Enabled, put each load's trace in its own folder,
.IR run- date-time /trace.log ,
beside the daemon log: a reader is started with the load and stopped
before the unload. It touches no service and needs no root. For
testing.
.SH [Boot]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
Installed copies only; a portable copy does not run at boot.
.TP
.BR FinishLeftover " (default 1)"
After a power loss or a crash while VLHE was loaded, the changes it
made are still on record. 1: the boot puts them back first - only what
VLHE recorded making, never a path someone changed since - and loads
VLHE if that worked. 0: the boot only notes it, and VLHE stays unloaded
until it is finished with
.B vlhe apply \-u
or Finish the unload on the Status page. Either way the next
.B vlhe status
or Status page says what happened, once.
.SH [Load]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
.TP
.BR BaselineDrift " (default ask)"
What a Load from the control centre or
.B vlhe apply
does when a device file VLHE manages, such as
.I /dev/dsp
or
.IR /dev/cdrom ,
has changed since VLHE recorded it, and VLHE did not change it.
.B ask
asks each time: undo the change, accept it as the new baseline, load
anyway, or cancel.
.B warn
keeps the baseline, leaves the change, loads, and says so.
.B refuse
stops the Load with nothing changed, and says why. The boot always
warns, since no one is there to answer, and so does
.B vlhe apply
when it is not run from a terminal. Set in the control centre under
File > Preferences, System Baseline.
.SH [Paths]
In
.IR /etc/vlhe.conf .
.TP
.BR ModuleDir " (not read)"
No longer used. An installed VLHE loads its modules with
.BR modprobe ,
which finds the running kernel's own copy in
.IR /lib/modules/ kernel /misc ,
so a machine that boots more than one 2.2.16 kernel loads the right
one for each. A portable VLHE uses its own
.I modules
folder. A file that still has the key is unaffected.
.SH [Interface]
In the user's file. The control centre.
.TP
.BR Font " (default empty)"
The control centre's font, as a full X font name, size included - as
File > Preferences writes it. Empty means GTK's default. This is how
to get larger text.
.B vlhe.gtk \-\-reset
clears it.
.TP
.BR StartPage " (default 0)"
The page the window opens on, and where OK returns to: 0 Status,
1 Volume, 2 Sound Settings, 3 Midi Settings, 4 CD Settings, 5 CD+G
Viewer, 6 Render MIDI.
.TP
.BR VerticalSliders " (default 0)"
Draw the Volume page's faders vertically.
.TP
.BR ShowApplyResult " (default empty)"
Show a box listing every step after Load or Unload. Empty: on for a
portable copy, off when installed. 1 always, 0 never.
.SH [Render Settings]
In the user's file. The Render MIDI page's Advanced tab. These reach
.BR smf2wav (1)
only and never change the synth.
.TP
.BR UseVlheSettings " (default 1)"
1 renders with the Midi Settings, so the file sounds as the machine
plays it; 0 uses the values below.
.TP
.BR Voices " (default 512)"
The most voices, 1 to 2048. A render has no deadline, so it can have
far more than the synth.
.TP
.BR Rate " (default 44100)"
The rendered file's sample rate.
.TP
.BR Gain " (default 500)"
The master gain in thousandths: 1000 unity, 2000 the most.
.TP
.BR Law " (default 0)"
0 the SoundFont standard, 1 the gentler Sound Blaster era curve.
.TP
.BR Filter " (default 0)"
0 AWE32, 1 SoundFont 2.01, 2 SoundFont 2.04, 3 none.
.TP
.BR Reverb " (default 1)"
The reverb for a render, 1 on, 0 off.
.TP
.BR Chorus " (default 1)"
The chorus for a render, 1 on, 0 off. These replace the
.B Effects
key, which is no longer read.
.TP
.BR Bypass " (default 0)"
Skip the low-pass filter where its cutoff is above anything the
sample carries, which makes rendering faster.
.TP
.BR ModEnv " (default 1)"
The modulation envelope for a render, as the Midi Settings key of the
same name: 1 fast, 0 reference. Identical on everything tested.
.TP
.BR GmFont " (default empty)"
The General MIDI font when UseVlheSettings is 0; empty means the Midi
Settings' own.
.TP
.BR SongFont " (default empty)"
A song font for bank 1, or empty for none.
.TP
.BR WavTemp " (default 0)"
Where the temporary WAV goes during an MP3 render; it is about ten
times the MP3's size. 0 whichever of
.I /tmp
and the output's folder has more free space, 1 always
.IR /tmp ,
2 always beside the output.
.TP
.BR Lame " (default empty)"
The path of the LAME program, for MP3 output. LAME is not part of
Corel Linux or of VLHE.
.SH [CDG Viewer]
In the user's file. The CD+G Viewer page.
.TP
.BR Zoom " (default 2)"
The picture's scale: 1 (300 x 216) or 2 (600 x 432). Whole numbers
only, because a fractional scale blurs the picture's tiles.
.TP
.BR Anchor " (default 5)"
Where the picture sits, as a numeric keypad: 7 8 9 along the top,
4 5 6 across the middle, 1 2 3 along the bottom. The controls stay at
the bottom. Detached, only left, centre or right is used.
.TP
.BR TrackFormat " (default 0)"
The track list: 0 the title alone, 1 artist and title, for a
compilation. 1 needs CD-TEXT, or a CUE sheet naming a performer for
each track.
.TP
.BR InfoFields " (default performer,title)"
The CD-TEXT fields on the line under the picture, in order, separated
by commas: any of
.BR title ,
.BR performer ,
.BR songwriter ,
.BR composer ,
.BR arranger ,
.BR message ,
.BR track ,
.BR time .
There is room for about 86 characters at Zoom 2.
.TP
.BR BorderMask " (default 1)"
Hide the picture's outer edge, as a CD+G player does.
.TP
.BR ClearOnEject " (default 1)"
Clear the picture when the disc is ejected; 0 keeps the last frame.
.TP
.BR Drive " (default 0)"
The drive the viewer shows and plays: 0 is
.IR /dev/vdisc0 .
.TP
.BR FollowAnyDisc " (default 1)"
1: when that drive has no disc with audio, use the first drive that
does. 0: that drive only.
.TP
.BR StopOnSwap " (default 0)"
1: choosing another drive stops the disc the viewer was playing.
A disc started from KsCD is never stopped.
.TP
.BR CompactDetached " (default 0)"
When the viewer is detached, put Attach and the track list on a
second row: a narrower window, one row taller.
.SH [Fonts]
In the user's file.
.TP
.BR Search " (default empty)"
More folders to look in for SoundFonts, separated by colons, searched
before the built-in ones:
.IR /usr/share/sounds/sf2 ,
.I /usr/local/share/sounds/sf2
and
.IR ~/.vlhe/sf2 .
.SH DRIVE STATE
.I /var/lib/vlhe/state/drives
is state rather than configuration: what is in each virtual drive.
The disc daemon writes it; the control centre asks the daemon rather
than writing it itself. Under
.BR [Drives] :
.TP
.BI Drive N
The image in drive
.IR N .
.TP
.BI Autoload N
1 if drive
.IR N 's
image comes back at the next load (Load at startup).
.TP
.B Cdrom
The drive
.I /dev/cdrom
reaches when LinkCdrom is on.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vlhe.conf
.TP
.I ~/.vlhe/vlhe.conf
.TP
.I ~/.vlhe/vlhe-draft.conf
.TP
.I /etc/vlhe/defaults.conf
.TP
.I /var/lib/vlhe/state/drives
.PP
As described above.
.SH BUGS
.B CardModule
has no effect.
